From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Sync go.mod with go-vendor-tools.toml pre_commands

go-vendor-tools.toml's [archive] pre_commands bumps go.mod's `go`
directive from 1.12 to 1.14 (Go's own vendor-consistency checking
defaults to `-mod=vendor` starting at 1.14, so older module directives
need this bump to avoid `go build` silently falling back to GOPATH mode
against a stale vendor tree) -- but that command only ever runs against
gorget's own fetch/vendor checkout, never against the actual %prep source
tree, which is built straight from the plain source tarball (Source0).

%prep can't just run the pre_command's `sed` directly: keeping it purely
textual like a patch is simpler than replicating a go-vendor-tools.toml
edit as a second, redundant %prep step, and this is the same treatment
already used for trivy's equivalent gap.

diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 module github.com/cpuguy83/go-md2man/v2
 
-go 1.12
+go 1.14
 
 require github.com/russross/blackfriday/v2 v2.1.0
